      "message": "Say which build is answering, and package a release the way one arrives\n\n`cairn --version` said 0.1.0 and nothing else, on every build since the\nfirst. It now names the version and the commit and date it was built\nfrom, stamped by core's build script from the checkout (CAIRN_BUILD\noverrides it for whoever packages from an archive); /healthz carries the\nsame string, `serve` logs it at start, and the watcher's record of an\nanswer includes it, so the question \"which build is that\" has an answer\nwherever it is asked. The workspace version becomes 0.1.0-alpha.1, since\nthat is what this is.\n\nscripts/release.sh builds for the machine it runs on and packages one\narchive with the binary, the licence and the README beside a SHA256SUMS,\nuploading both when a bucket is configured. The operating guide gains\nInstalling (from source, through this forge) and Upgrading (what a schema\nrebuild does and does not touch), and the README's try-it installs the\nbinary before it runs it. The first-run walk checks the version string\nfirst.\n\nChange-Id: Irelease0089version\nSigned-off-by: Mandip Adhikari <92096340+mandipadk@users.noreply.github.com>",
